  "findings": [
    "Base ResourcesManager initialization is the main measured cost: about25-30seconds, including about15-18seconds loading normal plant assets.",
    "UI constructor normally costs3.4-3.7seconds; the lazy constructor costs5-8milliseconds, with some menu loading moving into subsequent first use.",
    "Sound loading and data parsing are much smaller in these traces.",
    "Of3362original Texture2D assets, only13are readable (~3.1MiB serialized image data); disabling texture readability would not provide a meaningful general win.",
    "The stock game requests200FPS. That is not actual FPS, and this GPU-constrained emulator is already much slower; a forced cap is not an evidenced fix for its startup delay."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only two timing trials per mode; not a statistically broad hardware benchmark.",
    "The stock-Chinese marker is an Awake log, so its wall seconds must not be directly compared to the English frame-sample-and-memory endpoint.",
    "No physical-device testing, combat FPS improvement, thermal/power result or promise of solving the reporter2-3minute delay.",
    "First opening a deferred menu can pause while its prefab loads; later visits use its cached asset.",
    "Prototype owner tracking and fallback need hardening; runtime compatibility and save/profile lifecycle need release-level validation before production enablement.",
    "All94prefabs load correctly, but six menu families are smoke-tested, not every possible menu interaction."
  ],
  "next_targets": [
    "Retain this UI-loading candidate for next-release integration after hardening and device validation.",
    "Profile the much larger plant/skin/zombie preload phase before considering on-demand loading there; fusion, preview, skin and enumeration dependencies make it a larger change.",
    "Investigate frame pacing on real target hardware before adding any optional FPS policy."
  ],
